# Response headers for the Cloudflare Workers asset bundle (assets directory =
# ./static). The SPA has always carried these as <meta http-equiv=…>, but a meta
# tag cannot deliver every one of them: browsers ignore X-Frame-Options in meta,
# and frame-ancestors is disallowed in a meta-delivered policy. Delivered as
# headers they take effect, and they now cover the paths that never had them
# (admin.html and logistics.html declare no CSP at all, so only the universal
# headers below protect them).
#
# Cloudflare's own analytics beacon stays blocked by the policy below. Adding
# https://static.cloudflareinsights.com to script-src would enable it, which is a
# call about visitor tracking rather than a fix, so it is left alone.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains

/
